│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current algorithm sends every partition over a single Dijkstra shortest path, causing │
│                          │ redundant transfers over the same (possibly expensive) links and ignoring parallel        │
│                          │ network paths. A better strategy is to (1) enumerate multiple candidate paths per         │
│                          │ destination (k-shortest simple paths by cost), (2) split the partitions across those      │
│                          │ parallel paths proportionally to their achievable throughput so load is balanced across   │
│                          │ networks, and (3) prefer the set of paths that minimizes the weighted sum of per-GB cost. │
│                          │ This reduces redundant transfers over the same links, exploits multi-network topologies,  │
│                          │ and lowers total cost while keeping the BroadCastTopology structure intact (each          │
│                          │ partition gets exactly one path with its edge list). Edges missing cost data are given a  │
│                          │ large penalty so they are only used when necessary, and cached edge data is passed        │
│                          │ directly into the topology to avoid recomputation.                                        │
