│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multicloud_broadcast_optimization                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The current implementation naively computes the same single shortest path for every       │
│                          │ partition of every destination, causing redundant transfers over identical edges and      │
│                          │ overloading shared bottleneck links. To reduce total cost, we should:                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. For each (dst, partition) pair, use edge-disjoint (or at least diverse) shortest paths │
│                          │ via `nx.shortest_simple_paths`, so partitions of the same destination can be spread       │
│                          │ across different networks/clouds rather than duplicating the same path 4 times.           │
│                          │ 2. Avoid having all destinations route through the same cheap edges: when many flows      │
│                          │ already use an edge, artificially inflate its cost so subsequent searches are pushed to   │
│                          │ parallel paths, balancing load and exploiting the multi-network topology.                 │
│                          │ 3. Use a working copy of the graph with dynamically adjusted costs so overlapping         │
│                          │ transfers get penalized, reducing redundant transfers across destinations.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This yields lower overall data transfer cost by spreading broadcast traffic across        │
│                          │ parallel, diverse routes instead of stacking everything onto a single cheapest path.      │
