│ patch_description        │ The baseline assigns every partition the same single Dijkstra path, which both wastes     │
│                          │ cheaper parallel routes and concentrates load on a single network link. A better          │
│                          │ broadcast strategy: for each destination, compute the k-shortest simple paths (by cost).  │
│                          │ Distribute partitions across these candidate paths so that cheaper paths serve more       │
│                          │ partitions while more expensive alternates absorb the remaining partitions. This exploits │
│                          │ multi-network topologies (parallel paths), reduces redundant transfer volume on costly    │
│                          │ links, and balances load. We also cache candidate paths per destination to avoid          │
│                          │ recomputation overhead, and gracefully fall back to a single path when fewer alternatives │
│                          │ exist.                                                                                    │
