│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ steiner_tree_broadcast_routing                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current algorithm routes each destination independently with Dijkstra, and then       │
│                          │ replicates the exact same path for every partition. This causes massive redundant         │
│                          │ transfers: if two destinations share a path prefix, the data is sent over the same links  │
│                          │ multiple times, and each partition duplicates the whole route. A much cheaper broadcast   │
│                          │ structure is a Steiner tree: data is forwarded once over shared links and only splits     │
│                          │ where destinations diverge. I use the classic shortest-path-heuristic Steiner tree        │
│                          │ approximation (iteratively connect the nearest unconnected destination to the current     │
│                          │ tree), which yields a single low-cost multicast tree. Then I assign partitions to the     │
│                          │ tree edges, and to balance load across networks, partitions after the first are routed    │
│                          │ via alternative low-cost paths (k-shortest simple paths) when available, spreading        │
│                          │ traffic across parallel network links while keeping costs low. This reduces both          │
│                          │ redundant transfers (shared tree edges) and per-partition duplication cost, directly      │
│                          │ minimizing total data transfer cost.                                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0079                                                                                   │
