│ patch_name               │ multi_path_partition_split                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current algorithm sends every partition of every destination along the exact same     │
│                          │ single Dijkstra path, which overloads that route's throughput budget and ignores cheaper  │
│                          │ alternate routes. Instead, for each destination we enumerate the k cheapest simple paths  │
│                          │ (via `nx.shortest_simple_paths` ordered by cost) and assign each partition to a different │
│                          │ candidate path. This (1) spreads the transfer load across multiple parallel network       │
│                          │ routes so per-edge throughput limits are respected instead of being oversubscribed, and   │
│                          │ (2) allows some partitions to exploit alternate low-cost multi-network paths. If fewer    │
│                          │ than `num_partitions` simple paths exist, partitions wrap around over the available       │
│                          │ paths, preserving the original shortest-path behavior as a fallback.                      │
