│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ diverse_partition_paths_reuse_aware                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the naive per-dst Dijkstra path (replicated identically for every partition) with │
│                          │ a smarter strategy:                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Compute up to `num_partitions` diverse shortest-simple-paths per destination and rank  │
│                          │ them with a combined weight that favors cheap links shared across destinations (reuse     │
│                          │ reduces redundant transfers) and higher-throughput links (so partitions transfer in       │
│                          │ parallel rather than queueing on one bottleneck link).                                    │
│                          │ 2. Round-robin partitions across each destination's diverse paths, spreading load over    │
│                          │ multiple networks instead of dumping all partitions over a single path.                   │
│                          │ 3. Keep a Dijkstra fallback for robustness so all destinations remain reachable.          │
