│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ kshortest_partition_broadcast                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current algorithm sends every partition of every destination along the same single    │
│                          │ Dijkstra shortest path, causing all traffic to concentrate on one route. This new         │
│                          │ approach computes k-shortest simple paths (k=4) per destination using                     │
│                          │ nx.shortest_simple_paths with edge cost as weight, then distributes partitions across     │
│                          │ these candidate paths using a load-aware assignment: partitions are assigned round-robin  │
│                          │ to candidate paths ordered by cost, with per-edge congestion tracking (edge_load counter) │
│                          │ and a congestion penalty (edge cost + congestion_weight * load) to avoid overloading      │
│                          │ cheap links. This reduces total cost by exploiting alternate low-cost parallel routes and │
│                          │ balancing load across multi-network topologies. Key parameters: K_PATHS=4 candidate paths │
│                          │ per destination, CONGESTION_WEIGHT=0.5 penalty per concurrent use of an edge, and         │
│                          │ round-robin partition assignment instead of duplicating a single path.                    │
