│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ steiner_fanout_multiflow                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of routing every partition of every destination independently along the same      │
│                          │ shortest path (which piles num_partitions × N flows onto one route and overloads its      │
│                          │ throughput constraint), this approach treats the broadcast as a group routing problem. It │
│                          │ computes k-shortest diverse paths per destination, then assigns partitions across those   │
│                          │ paths to balance load — like a multi-commodity fanout. It also builds a shared            │
│                          │ Steiner-tree-inspired "trunk" so destinations with overlapping routes reuse edges,        │
│                          │ reducing redundant transfers. Edge costs are weighted by cost/available_throughput to     │
│                          │ prefer cheap, uncongested links, and load across parallel edges is spread so per-edge     │
│                          │ flow stays below throughput.                                                              │
