│ patch_name               │ steiner_tree_broadcast_paths                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Replace per-destination independent shortest paths with a shared Steiner tree approach.   │
│                          │ Broadcast data can be split across parallel paths: instead of sending all partitions of   │
│                          │ every destination along the same Dijkstra path (which duplicates transfers on shared      │
│                          │ links), we compute a low-cost Steiner tree connecting src to all dsts. Shared edges only  │
│                          │ need to be traversed once per partition, drastically reducing redundant transfers. For    │
│                          │ each partition, we use k-shortest-path candidates on the Steiner tree / residual graph to │
│                          │ spread load and use parallel paths, balancing throughput. This reduces total cost (fewer  │
│                          │ redundant edge traversals) and improves load balance.                                     │
