│ patch_description        │ The original algorithm routes every partition of every destination along a single         │
│                          │ shortest path, causing redundant transfers over shared edges. Inspired by                 │
│                          │ multicast/Steiner-tree ideas and k-shortest-path load balancing, this approach: (1)       │
│                          │ computes k candidate shortest paths per destination, (2) balances partitions across those │
│                          │ candidate paths to spread load and exploit parallel low-cost links, and (3) prefers edges │
│                          │ shared with already-planned routes (cheap "piggybacking" on transfers already scheduled), │
│                          │ reducing redundant data movement. The result is lower total cost while keeping the same   │
│                          │ BroadCastTopology output format.                                                          │
