│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ steiner_broadcast_mst                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of routing each destination independently with Dijkstra (which re-sends data over │
│                          │ shared edges once per destination), this approach treats the broadcast as a directed      │
│                          │ Steiner tree problem: it computes a union subgraph of low-cost paths from src to all      │
│                          │ destinations, then repeatedly contracts shared edges so that the source's data only needs │
│                          │ to be transferred once along shared trunk links. For each destination, we run Dijkstra on │
│                          │ a "shared-cost" metric where an edge already carrying data to another destination is      │
│                          │ discounted (cost multiplied by a small factor), encouraging paths to reuse existing trunk │
│                          │ edges. This reduces redundant transfers across common cloud backbone links and directly   │
│                          │ lowers total data transfer cost. All partitions for a destination follow the same shared  │
│                          │ tree path, keeping the structure simple and robust (Dijkstra fallback guarantees no       │
│                          │ failures).                                                                                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
