│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ greedy_onesided_krouter                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Restructure the routing into a modular CandidateRouter that, for each destination,        │
│                          │ computes the Dijkstra baseline path (exact fallback, guaranteeing correctness) and        │
│                          │ compares it against a small set of k-shortest candidate paths. A candidate is adopted     │
│                          │ only if it is strictly cheaper than the Dijkstra baseline (one-sided greedy improvement), │
│                          │ minimizing risk while opening the door to lower-cost routes through multi-hop network     │
│                          │ paths. Dijkstra results are cached so shared destinations are never recomputed, and edge  │
│                          │ costs are read from a single safe accessor that tolerates missing cost data. This keeps   │
│                          │ the output format identical while reducing total transfer cost wherever cheaper alternate │
│                          │ paths exist.                                                                              │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
