│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_edge_reuse_multicast                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Treat the broadcast as a multicast (Steiner-tree-like) problem rather than independent    │
│                          │ per-destination shortest paths. Total cost depends on the union of edges used, so if a    │
│                          │ later destination can reach an already-delivered intermediate node cheaply and then reuse │
│                          │ an already-paid edge prefix, the overall cost drops. Concretely: route destinations       │
│                          │ sequentially; after each destination is routed, mark its edges as "paid". For subsequent  │
│                          │ destinations, run Dijkstra on a reduced-cost graph where paid edges cost ~0 marginal      │
│                          │ (small epsilon to prefer shorter reuse), so routing strongly prefers reusing existing     │
│                          │ broadcast edges. This creates a shared multicast tree instead of parallel per-destination │
│                          │ paths, reducing redundant transfers and total cost.                                       │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
