│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ bounded_kshortest_paths                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses a single Dijkstra shortest path per destination, repeated for    │
│                          │ all partitions. This can be suboptimal when another destination's cheapest path is        │
│                          │ slightly more expensive but avoids a shared trunk that the first path already saturates,  │
│                          │ or when parallel paths allow cheaper per-partition routing. I propose enumerating a       │
│                          │ bounded set of k-shortest simple paths (k=4) per destination using a generator (never     │
│                          │ materializing all paths), then greedily assigning each partition to the cheapest          │
│                          │ candidate path under a congestion penalty that accumulates as partitions are assigned.    │
│                          │ This reduces redundant transfers by spreading partitions across parallel paths, balances  │
│                          │ load across networks, and exploits multi-network topologies to minimize total cost, while │
│                          │ staying within the Gen 9 safety bound (4-8 candidates preserves 100% success).            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
