│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ expensive_dsts_first_reuse                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Process destinations in descending order of their baseline Dijkstra path cost. The most   │
│                          │ expensive destinations build the expensive trunk edges first; subsequent                  │
│                          │ (shorter/cheaper) destinations can then route through those already-paid-for edges at     │
│                          │ zero marginal cost via the existing reuse-aware scoring. This maximizes the shared-trunk  │
│                          │ discount effect without any structural changes — only the iteration order of the          │
│                          │ destination loop changes. We precompute each destination's baseline Dijkstra cost (with   │
│                          │ the same edge_cost function so missing costs are penalized) and iterate sorted            │
│                          │ descending, falling back to original order for unreachable destinations.                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
