│ patch_name               │ safe_none_cost_fallback_with_shared_reuse                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current best (1035.14) routes only on the cost-valid view and ignores None-cost edges │
│                          │ entirely; Gen 2 (1021.03) showed that k-shortest candidates plus shared-edge reuse across │
│                          │ partitions lowers cost. This edit combines both insights safely: (1) compute a baseline   │
│                          │ path on the cost-valid subgraph via Dijkstra, (2) compute an alternative path on the full │
│                          │ graph where None-cost edges are given the median observed edge cost as a neutral default  │
│                          │ — never a huge penalty — and (3) adopt the alternative only if its strictly-evaluated     │
│                          │ valid-graph cost is lower, preserving the "never worse than baseline" invariant. Edge     │
│                          │ reuse across partitions is tracked in `shared_edges` so already-paid edges cost ~0 when   │
│                          │ scoring subsequent destinations, reducing redundant transfers across the broadcast.       │
