╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_trunk_multicast_discount                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current algorithm routes each destination independently with Dijkstra, ignoring that  │
│                          │ broadcast traffic shares trunks across destinations. Prior attempts at per-destination    │
│                          │ path diversification failed, but cross-destination trunk consolidation has never been     │
│                          │ validly tested. The idea: process destinations sequentially, maintaining a `used_edges`   │
│                          │ set of (src, dst) node pairs already routed. For each destination, enumerate a small      │
│                          │ number (≤6) of bounded candidate simple paths via `nx.shortest_simple_paths` (a           │
│                          │ generator, so only the first few paths are materialized — cheap). Score each candidate as │
│                          │ `true_cost - alpha * (cost of candidate edges already in used_edges)`, where alpha ≈ 0.3. │
│                          │ Pick the candidate with the minimum discounted score, but only adopt it if its true cost  │
│                          │ is ≤ the pure Dijkstra baseline cost. This guarantees we are never worse than the current │
│                          │ proven baseline (1035.14), while allowing reuse of already-paid-for trunks to guide       │
│                          │ selection when multiple equal/near-equal routes exist — encouraging consolidation onto    │
│                          │ shared multicast trees, which reduces redundant transfers. Costs are guarded with         │
│                          │ `.get("cost") or 0` for robustness, and exceptions for unreachable nodes fall back to     │
│                          │ baseline behavior, preserving the 100% success rate.                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0075                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
