│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ fix_baseline_cost_computation                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current code that orders destinations by baseline Dijkstra cost computes the cost     │
│                          │ incorrectly: it calls `edge_cost(h[path][path], h[path][path])`, passing the same         │
│                          │ edge-data dict twice instead of the (u, v, data) signature. While `edge_cost` ignores u,v │
│                          │ and reads `d.get("cost")`, the double-call pattern is fragile and the accumulation is     │
│                          │ convoluted. A cleaner and more robust approach is `nx.dijkstra_path_length(h, src, dst,   │
│                          │ weight=edge_cost)`, which directly returns the exact baseline cost. Additionally, the     │
│                          │ shared-edge discount currently only reuses trunks opportunistically via candidate         │
│                          │ enumeration (k=4 simple paths). To better exploit trunks built by earlier (expensive)     │
│                          │ destinations, we increase the candidate pool from 4 to 8, giving later destinations more  │
│                          │ chances to latch onto already-paid shared edges at zero marginal cost. Both changes       │
│                          │ reduce total transfer cost with no structural risk.                                       │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
