│ patch_name               │ greedy_shared_edge_ordering                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Improve on the k-candidate approach by: (1) processing destinations in order of           │
│                          │ decreasing baseline Dijkstra cost so expensive destinations build shared trunk edges that │
│                          │ later (cheaper) destinations reuse for free, and (2) replacing the fixed set of k         │
│                          │ candidates with an exact Dijkstra run on a dynamically re-weighted graph where            │
│                          │ already-paid (shared) edges cost ~0. This is a classic greedy Steiner-tree heuristic for  │
│                          │ multicast/broadcast: it minimizes marginal cost per destination instead of independent    │
│                          │ shortest paths. Costs remain on valid edges only (None-cost edges penalized), preserving  │
│                          │ the 100% success rate while cutting redundant transfers.                                  │
