│ patch_description        │ Process destinations in descending order of baseline Dijkstra path cost when applying     │
│                          │ reuse discounts. Long, expensive routes have the most shared-trunk potential; routing     │
│                          │ them first builds up the set of used edges so that later, shorter destinations can latch  │
│                          │ onto already-built trunks at a discount. This is a low-risk mutation of the loop          │
│                          │ iteration order: we pre-compute baseline paths/costs, sort destinations by descending     │
│                          │ baseline cost, and then run the existing reuse-aware candidate selection in that order.   │
