│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ greedy_steiner_dyn_reweight                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The best prior result (749.49 vs current 1035.14) came from a greedy Steiner-tree         │
│                          │ heuristic: process destinations in order of decreasing standalone Dijkstra cost, and      │
│                          │ re-run Dijkstra per destination with dynamic edge weights where already-paid (shared)     │
│                          │ edges count as free. This builds shared trunk edges early and lets later destinations     │
│                          │ piggyback at zero marginal cost, minimizing the union of paid edges — which the evaluator │
│                          │ charges once globally per (dst, partition)-independent edge. The current program lost     │
│                          │ that sharing logic. I restore the dynamic re-weighting approach and additionally keep the │
│                          │ destination ordering (expensive first) so trunks are built by the destinations that       │
│                          │ benefit most. I also keep a safe fallback to `shortest_path` for disconnected nodes,      │
│                          │ preserving the 100% success rate.                                                         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
