│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ lookahead_shared_trunk_routing                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ This version implements a shared-trunk routing strategy: (1) destinations are processed   │
│                          │ in a greedy "expensive-first" order so that costly destinations get to choose their paths │
│                          │ first and cheap destinations can then piggyback on the already-used shared edges; (2) for │
│                          │ each destination, k-shortest candidate paths are scored against a set of `shared_edges`   │
│                          │ already emitted by earlier destinations, where reuse of shared edges counts as free       │
│                          │ (never a discount, only full reuse), strongly biasing later routes onto a common trunk;   │
│                          │ (3) a one-step lookahead is applied: candidates for remaining destinations are pre-scored │
│                          │ against a hypothetical future trunk (current shared edges plus edges used by other        │
│                          │ already-scored candidates), so the router prefers edges that multiple other destinations  │
│                          │ will also want, forming a shared backbone early. Baseline Dijkstra paths are always       │
│                          │ included as candidates, guaranteeing valid fallbacks and no regressions versus the naive  │
│                          │ algorithm.                                                                                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
