│ patch_name               │ planner_trunk_reuse_crossover                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the PathPlanner-based approach and the trunk-reuse (alpha discount)          │
│                          │ approach. The new program: (1) builds a valid-graph restricted to known-cost edges plus a │
│                          │ full graph with median-filled None costs for candidate discovery (from the PathPlanner    │
│                          │ parent); (2) processes destinations in descending order of baseline cost so expensive     │
│                          │ routes build shared trunks first (from the alpha-discount parent); (3) scores candidate   │
│                          │ paths with a reuse discount on edges already used by other destinations, encouraging      │
│                          │ shared edges that reduce redundant transfers; (4) adopts a path only if its true valid    │
│                          │ cost never exceeds the Dijkstra baseline, guaranteeing it is never worse than all prior   │
│                          │ programs; (5) retains the safe full-graph fallback when cost filtering disconnects a      │
│                          │ destination. Interface (inputs/outputs) is unchanged.                                     │
